#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:336
msgid ""
"The most common source of confusion is **Force Guest Customization** — "
"this setting works on VMware/VME (via VMware Tools) and HVM (via the "
"guest agent). On public clouds (AWS, Azure), customization is handled by "
"the cloud provider's metadata service and this setting has no effect."
msgstr "La fuente más común de confusión es **Force Guest Customization** — este ajuste funciona en VMware/VME (mediante VMware Tools) y HVM (mediante el agente del guest). En nubes públicas (AWS, Azure), la personalización la gestiona el servicio de metadatos del proveedor de nube y este ajuste no tiene efecto."

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:340
msgid ""
"**ISO image types** — When uploading ISO images (used for manual OS "
"installations or boot media), disable both **Cloud Init Enabled** and "
"**Enabled Sysprep**. ISO-based images are typically booted interactively "
"for OS installation and do not use cloud-init or sysprep-based guest "
"customization. Leaving these options enabled on an ISO image will cause "
"provisioning failures or unexpected behavior."
msgstr "**Tipos de imagen ISO** — Al cargar imágenes ISO (utilizadas para instalaciones manuales del SO o medios de arranque), deshabilite tanto **Cloud Init Enabled** como **Enabled Sysprep**. Las imágenes basadas en ISO normalmente se arrancan de forma interactiva para la instalación del SO y no utilizan cloud-init ni personalización del guest basada en sysprep. Dejar estas opciones habilitadas en una imagen ISO provocará fallos de aprovisionamiento o comportamiento inesperado."

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:342
msgid ""
"For HVM, provision the VM from the ISO, complete the installer through "
"the VM console, eject the ISO media, and restart the VM from its "
"installed disk. For the related HVM boot controls and the separate "
"network-boot path, see "
":doc:`/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/vm_advanced_options`."
msgstr "Para HVM, aprovisione la VM desde la ISO, complete el instalador a través de la consola de la VM, expulse el medio ISO y reinicie la VM desde su disco instalado. Para los controles de arranque HVM relacionados y la ruta de arranque por red separada, consulte :doc:`/infrastructure/clusters/hvm/vm_advanced_options`."

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:345
msgid "Import an HVM Instance as an Image"
msgstr "Importar una instancia HVM como imagen"

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:347
msgid ""
"Before selecting :guilabel:`Actions` > :guilabel:`Import as Image` for an"
" HVM VM installed from ISO, verify that the guest boots from its "
"installed disk and eject the installation ISO. The import excludes ISO "
"volumes and exports the installed disks."
msgstr "Antes de seleccionar :guilabel:`Actions` > :guilabel:`Import as Image` para una VM HVM instalada desde ISO, verifique que el guest arranque desde su disco instalado y expulse la ISO de instalación. La importación excluye volúmenes ISO y exporta los discos instalados."

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:349
msgid ""
"Existing file-based snapshots do not need to be deleted before import. "
"When a disk has a qcow2 backing chain, |morpheus| copies and merges the "
"chain into a temporary export disk without modifying the VM's existing "
"snapshots. Other supported storage backends create their own temporary "
"export snapshot."
msgstr "Los snapshots basados en archivos existentes no necesitan eliminarse antes de la importación. Cuando un disco tiene una cadena de respaldo qcow2, |morpheus| copia y fusiona la cadena en un disco de exportación temporal sin modificar los snapshots existentes de la VM. Otros backends de almacenamiento compatibles crean su propio snapshot de exportación temporal."

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:351
msgid ""
"After the import finishes, verify that the resulting Virtual Image "
"contains ``metadata.json`` and every disk file referenced by the "
"manifest. A Virtual Image record or metadata file without the referenced "
"disk files is incomplete, even if its status is Active. Leave the source "
"VM and snapshots unchanged and contact Support with the HVM version, "
"storage backend, snapshot list, and import process output. Deleting an "
"existing snapshot is not a required import step and should not be used as"
" an import workaround."
msgstr "Después de que finalice la importación, verifique que la imagen virtual resultante contenga ``metadata.json`` y cada archivo de disco referenciado por el manifiesto. Un registro de imagen virtual o archivo de metadatos sin los archivos de disco referenciados está incompleto, incluso si su estado es Activo. Deje la VM de origen y los snapshots sin cambios y contacte con Soporte con la versión HVM, backend de almacenamiento, lista de snapshots y salida del proceso de importación. Eliminar un snapshot existente no es un paso requerido de importación y no debe utilizarse como solución alternativa de importación."

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:354
msgid "VMware - VM Templates Copies"
msgstr "VMware - VM Templates Copies"

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:356
msgid ""
"In a VMware environment, you may have a single VM template that you use "
"across different vCenters. Uploading an image to |morpheus|, mentioned in"
" the Add Virtual Image section, is one method to solve this. "
"Alternatively, an organization may decide to create a VM template in one "
"vCenter and then transfer it to other vCenters, which then could be "
"sync’d into |morpheus|."
msgstr ""
"In un/una VMware environment, you puede/n tienen un/una single VM "
"template ese/esa you use across diferente vCenters. Uploading un/una "
"image a |morpheus|, mentioned en el/la Add Imagen virtual section, es one"
" method a solve this. Alternatively, un/una organization puede/n decide a"
" create un/una VM template en one vCenter y entonces transfer it a "
"otro/otra vCenters, el/la cual entonces could be sync’d en |morpheus|."

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:358
msgid ""
"If all the vCenters are added as Clouds into |morpheus| and the templates"
" are named the same in each vCenter, they will be aggregated under a "
"single virtual image in |morpheus|. This means that as you deploy to the "
"various vCenter Clouds in |morpheus| using this virtual image, it will "
"choose the correct VM template to use based on the Cloud deployed to."
msgstr ""
"Si all the vCenters are added as Nubes into |morpheus| and the templates "
"are named the same in each vCenter, they will be aggregated under a "
"single virtual image in |morpheus|. This means that as you deploy to the "
"various vCenter Nubes in |morpheus| using this virtual image, it will "
"choose the correct VM template to use based on the Nube deployed to."

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:360
msgid ""
"This eliminates the need for creating multiple Node Types for each "
"virtual image if the templates were named differently in each vCenter. "
"This can reduce the overhead of maintaining multiple Node Types and "
"reduces user selections. As well, this can reduce the cloning time of VMs"
" by avoiding network transfers of images between geographic locations, "
"ensuring the closest VM template is selected."
msgstr ""
"Este/Esta eliminates el/la need para creating multiple Tipos de nodo para"
" cada virtual image si el/la templates fueron named differently en cada "
"vCenter. Este/Esta puede/n reduce el/la overhead de maintaining multiple "
"Tipos de nodo y reduces user selections. As well, este/esta puede/n "
"reduce el/la cloning time de VMs por avoiding network transfers de images"
" entre geographic locations, ensuring el/la closest VM template es "
"selected."

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:362
msgid ""
"|morpheus| supports VMware Content Libraries storing VM templates and "
"syncing into |morpheus|, the same as a template in a folder. "
"Additionally, the Content Library can be used to house the same template "
"in multiple libraries. If they have the same name, these templates will "
"be aggregated under a single virtual image. If the Content Library is "
"stored on a datastore that the target host/cluster has access to, it will"
" use that library first, to reduce the cloning time. If the Content "
"Library is not stored in a datastore accessible by the cluster/host, a "
"copy of the VM template will be performed to the target host/cluster "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| supports VMware Content Libraries storing VM templates and "
"syncing into |morpheus|, the same as a template in a folder. "
"Additionally, the Content Library puede ser used to house the same "
"template in multiple libraries. If they have the same name, these "
"templates will be aggregated under a single virtual image. If the Content"
" Library is stored on a datastore that the target host/cluster has access"
" to, it will use that library first, to reduce the cloning time. If the "
"Content Library is not stored in a datastore accessible by the "
"cluster/host, a copy of the VM template will be performed to the target "
"host/cluster instead."

#: ../../library/virtual_images/virtual_images.rst:364
msgid ""
"VM templates are a **Data Center** level object.  The same process above "
"applies to a single VMware cloud with multiple logical data centers.  It "
"will not apply to clusters, as a template is not associated with a "
"cluster, only when it is converted to a VM."
msgstr ""
"VM templates son un/una **Data Center** level object. El/La mismo/misma "
"process arriba applies a un/una single VMware cloud con multiple logical "
"data centers. It será/n ningún apply a clusters, como un/una template es "
"ningún asociado/asociada con un/una cluster, solo cuando it es converted "
"a un/una VM."

